commit d03427f ("Require Git::Native 0.006 for the fetch prune offset") bumps cpanfile's Git::Native pin from 0.005 to 0.006 to fix a real memory-safety bug: on libgit2 1.9 the embedded callbacks struct grew from 120 to 128 bytes, so the old prune-offset constant (derived from libgit2 1.5) wrote the prune flag 8 bytes early, landing on the update_refs callback pointer libgit2 1.9 prefers over update_tips instead of git_fetch_options.prune. App::karr::Git::_fetch_refspecs reads the fetch Result's ->updated to decide what a sync moved, so this could misreport what a fetch changed.

This is user-visible (cpanfile requirement bump + a real correctness/safety fix) and is not mentioned anywhere in the {{$NEXT}} section of Changes, unlike sibling commits from the same window (#257, #240, #228, #196) which explicitly note 'No Changes entry' with a reason. This one carries no such note -- looks like a plain oversight.

Found during the pre-0.600-release audit (karr-release-checker), cross-checking git log 0.500..HEAD against Changes.
